id: pm-rust-27da
title: "A float in item metadata hashes differently from the published CLI, and two doc contracts describe behaviour the code does not have"
description: "Three findings from CodeRabbit that had no reply. The hash: stable_json rendered numbers with serde_json, which writes a whole-valued f64 as 30.0 where JSON.stringify writes 30. Any item carrying a float in its metadata therefore produced a different before_hash and after_hash than the published CLI, which reads downstream as a corrupt history chain rather than as a formatting disagreement. The docs: COMPATIBILITY.md listed create as failing fast on a live lock and not implementing the wait budget, while the supported list above it said every mutation retries the budget and create_item does call acquire_lock with settings.locks. workspace.rs said an update requires at least one field to change, while update_item only tests presence, so setting a field to the value it already holds is accepted and writes a history record."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:conformance","area:history","review:coderabbit","type:defect"
created_at: "2026-08-28T06:09:05.835Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T06:09:22.958Z"
deadline: "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T06:09:22.942Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T06:09:22.942Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A whole-valued float and the same integer produce identical document hashes; exponent-form values render as JSON.stringify renders them; the renderer contains no unreachable branch; COMPATIBILITY.md no longer contradicts itself about the create lock wait budget; the update docstring states presence rather than change; coverage stays at 100 percent on every metric.
resolution: "stable_json routes Value::Number through javascript_number, which renders a finite whole-valued float below 1e21 without a decimal point and leaves everything else to serde_json, whose exponent form already matches. COMPATIBILITY.md's stale create exclusion is gone and workspace.rs states presence rather than change."
expected_result: "An item carrying a float in its metadata hashes identically on the native and published sides, and both documents describe what the code does."
actual_result: "Removing the Value::Number arm makes a whole-valued float and the same integer hash differently and the test fails; restoring it passes. Gates: cargo fmt --check 0, clippy -D warnings 0, cargo test 139 passed 0 failed, rustdoc with -D missing-docs 0, llvm-cov --branch 100.00 percent regions / functions / lines / branches."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rust-u4al,related,"2026-08-28T06:09:05.835Z",claude,"cli:create:dep",asserted
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:09:05.835Z",claude,"Non-vacuity at the digest level: removing the Value::Number arm makes a whole-valued float and the same integer hash to 1517ee47... and 61849ffe... respectively; restoring it makes them identical."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:09:05.835Z",claude,"Measured against node: JSON.stringify(30.0) is 30,JSON.stringify(1e21) is 1e+21,JSON.stringify(1e-7) is 1e-7. serde_json already signs exponents identically,so only the whole-valued case diverges and an exponent branch would have been unreachable code dressed as a safeguard."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T06:09:05.835Z",claude,A bot marking its own finding addressed is not evidence it was addressed. This one said addressed in commits a0df8fa to dc1c2bd and the scalar branch still had no normalisation.
